    "body": "The \\`ci-changes\\` output of the \\`file-changes\\` job compares \\`negative-files_count < any-files_count\\`. Step outputs are always strings, and GitHub Actions compares two strings lexicographically, so the result is wrong whenever the counts have a different number of digits.\n\nExample: #8123 changes 11 files, 2 of them under \\`Demos/benchmarks/**\\`. \\`'2' < '11'\\` evaluates to false, so \\`ci-changes\\` was false and \\`ci-early\\` / \\`ci-all\\` were skipped, while \\`ci-early-success\\` / \\`ci-success\\` still reported success.\n\nThis wraps both counts in \\`fromJSON()\\` so they are compared as numbers.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
    "closed_at": "2026-11-14T13:23:59Z",
